  | The Forgotten Archive                                  |
  |                                                        |
  | Dust covers every surface. Scrolls older than the      |
  | dungeon itself line the walls.                         |
  |                                                        |
  | This place was built by the original architects.       |
  |                                                        |
  | Somewhere in the dungeon, a fragment of their          |
  | knowledge remains hidden.                              |
  |                                                        |
  | To find it, you will need a new tool.                  |
  | Return to the entrance and use:                        |
  |                                                        |
  | « find . -name '*.fragment' »                          |
  |                                                        |
  | The 'find' command searches through every room         |
  | and passage, uncovering what the eye cannot see.       |
  | The dot means: start searching from here.              |
  |                                                        |
  | Find the fragment. Read it. Then return here           |
  | and speak the word of power to the sealed tome.        |
